ull,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.04723721136382486,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.34422978913168123,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01208,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":8.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Xencor, Inc., a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company, focuses on the discovery and development of engineered antibodies for the treatment of cancer and autoimmune diseases. The company provides Ultomiris to treat patients with atypical hemolytic uremic syndrome, generalized myasthenia gravis, and neuromyelitis optica spectrum disororder; and Monjuvi for the treatment of patients with relapsed or refractory diffuse large B-cell lymphoma. It also develops XmAb819, a bispecific antibody to treat renal cell carcinoma; XmAb541, which is in Phase I for the treatment of ovarian cancer; XmAb808, a bispecific antibody that binds to the broadly expressed tumor antigen; XmAb942, which is in clinical development for patients with Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis; Plamotamab, a bispecific T-cell, which is in Phase Ib study to treat rheumatoid arthritis; and XmAb657 for patients with idiopathic inflammatory myopathies. Further, the company develops Xaluritamig, a bispecific T-cell engager that treats prostate cancer; ASP2138 to treat gastric, gastroesophageal junction, and pancreatic cancers; JNJ-9401 to treat metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer; Obexelimab, an antibody to treat patients with autoimmune diseases; Tobevibart, a treatment for chronic hepatitis Delta; Zaltenibart to treat paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria and other alternative pathway disorders; Teropavimab and zinlirvimab to treat human immunodeficiency virus; Novartis, an antibody drug candidate that uses XmAb Fc technologies; and JNJ-1493 to treat B-cell malignancies. The company was incorporated in 1997 and is headquartered in Pasadena, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Bassil I. Dahiyat Ph.D. | Co-Founder, CEO, President & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 260 people. Revenue per employee of $483K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 18%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $166K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Xencor, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.7B market cap on $126M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -9% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -21% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $138M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -5.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 34% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (23.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 142% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8110919650264843},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 209% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Xencor (XNCR) Stock Could Be Overvalued On Q3 Earnings Beat","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-xncr/xencor